 "text": "9/29/26, 10:15 AM\ne The creditworthiness factor in percent\n\ne Manual creditworthiness\n\ne Number of dunning notices, returns, and write-offs\n\nThe creditworthiness figure is adjusted if a dunning notice or return is reversed.\n\nPrerequisites\n\nTime-Dependent Weighting\n\nTo determine the weighted total, enter a time-dependent creditworthiness weighting in Customizing for Contract Accounts\nReceivable and Payable under |}Business Transactions \u00bb Dunning 3 and/or |}Returns \u00bb Define Time-Dependent\nCreditworthiness Weightings\n\nDunning\n\nIf you want to use scoring, enter the dunning activities and/or dunning charges in conjunction with a creditworthiness figure. The\ndunning activity run reads the current creditworthiness of a business partner and selects the dunning activity and dunning charge\nwhere the creditworthiness determined is greater or the same as the creditworthiness value defined in Customizing.\n\nYou can define a creditworthiness weighting in the dunning levels of dunning procedures. Once dunning has taken place, the\ncreditworthiness figure of the current month is increased by this number.\n\nYou can define the creditworthiness figure in each dunning procedure and dunning level (in Customizing for Contract Accounts\n\nReceivable and Payable under |}Business Transactions \u00bb Dunning \u00bb Configure Dunning Activities 5 and Configure Charge\nSchedules for Dunning Procedure).\n\nReturns\n\nIf you want to use scoring, enter the returns activities in conjunction with a creditworthiness figure. During returns processing, the\ncreditworthiness of a business partner is determined automatically, and, depending on this creditworthiness among other things,\n\nthe returns activity where the creditworthiness value determined is greater or the same as the value defined in Customizing is\nselected.\n\nYou can define a credit weighting in the returns reasons. Once returns processing has taken place, the creditworthiness figure of\nthe current month is increased by this figure.\n\nYou can define the creditworthiness weighting with the returns reason in Customizing (see Customizing for Contract Accounts\nReceivable and Payable under |}Business Transactions \u00bb Returns \u00bb Configure Returns Reasons 3).\n\nWrite-Offs\n\nWrite-offs can also have a negative effect on a customer's creditworthiness. If you want to use scoring, enter the write-offs in\nconjunction with a creditworthiness score.\n\nYou can define the creditworthiness weighting with the write-off reasons in Customizing (see Customizing for Contract Accounts\nReceivable and Payable under |Business Transactions \u00bb Write-Offs \u00bb Configure Write-Off Reasons 3).\n\nInstallment Plan\n",
